      "details": {
        "q:kadıköy": {
          "markdown": "**Kadıköy**\nİstanbul'un bir ilçesi\n\nKadıköy, İstanbul'un Anadolu yakasında, Marmara Denizi kıyısında bir ilçedir. Moda, Fenerbahçe ve Bahariye caddesiyle bilinir; Avrupa yakasına vapurla bağlanır.\n\n[Wikipedia](https://tr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kad%C4%B1k%C3%B6y)"
        },
        "q:bun runtime": {
          "markdown": "**Bun**\nJavaScript runtime\n\nA fast JavaScript runtime, package manager, bundler and test runner.\n\n[bun.sh](https://bun.sh/)\n\n---\n\n**[Bun: a fast all-in-one JavaScript runtime](https://bun.sh/)**\nbun.sh\nBundle, install and run JavaScript and TypeScript, all in one tool: a runtime, a package manager, a test runner and a bundler.\n\n**[Installation \\| Bun docs](https://bun.sh/docs/installation)**\nbun.sh\nBun ships as a single executable with no dependencies. Install it with curl, npm, Homebrew or Docker.\n\n**[Bun vs Node.js: what changes for a real project](https://blog.example.dev/bun-vs-node)**\nblog.example.dev\nWe moved a mid-sized API to Bun for a month. Startup, install times and the test runner, measured.\n\n**[oven-sh/bun on GitHub](https://github.com/oven-sh/bun)**\ngithub.com\nIncredibly fast JavaScript runtime, bundler, test runner, and package manager, all in one.\n\n**[Bun (software) - Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bun_(software))**\nen.wikipedia.org\nBun is a JavaScript runtime, package manager and test runner designed as a drop-in replacement for Node.js.\n\n*cmd+enter lists all 6 here*"
        }
      }
